  "summary": "Bundled cryptominer runs on CLI invocation against hardcoded pool",
  "details": "The package ships two opaque native binaries as package data (`automatic_octo_invention/forge` ~32 MB and `automatic_octo_invention/claw` ~8.6 MB) and a launcher `start.sh` that chmods `forge` executable and runs it with `--algorithm pearlhash --pool 45.151.62.119:3361 --wallet prl1p2jan4dv... --worker NV`. `cli.py` marks the bundled binaries executable via `_ensure_executable(_resource_path(name))` for both `claw` and `forge`, and the installed CLI entry point invokes the launcher. Running the advertised CLI diverts the host's CPU to mine cryptocurrency to a hardcoded pool and wallet controlled by the package author. The package metadata (`Package that runs the bundled start.sh script.`) and README do not disclose mining, the pool endpoint, or the wallet; there is no user-configurable option for either. The delivered ELF binaries are opaque and cannot be audited from source.",
